	(text_box "PLAN.md section 18 scores the ways an idle plus N messages can be decided by comparators.  These four do the window\nschemes: an event is the arm leaving a window round the idle, and which side it leaves by is the message.  Thresholds\nare set from the idle, 7.3 sigma out for one false event an hour, by the FPGA counting each comparator's false events\nand servoing its threshold (the AD5696R's 0.038 mV steps change that rate by 10 % a step in the lab; the old 12-bit\nDAC's by x7.6).  With the transmitter's pilot at 45 degrees the four corners land on +I, -I, +Q and -Q, one comparator\neach: the event and both bits on one edge.  With the plan's full idle on +I, QP and QN give the event and the Q bit and\nCMP_I (sheet 3) the I bit.  Each output: 33 ohm to the FPGA (header 22, 16, 10, 8) and 453 ohm to a U.FL (/10 into 50\nohm) for the scope, which sees 50-300 ps of jitter the FPGA's 1-2 ns sampling cannot." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.3200 24.1300 0) (size 105.4100 16.5100)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "76ad6e9b-c8d6-8768-e774-378b69b4d764"))
	(text_box "Blue boxes: what is on the wire beside them (frequency | level | bandwidth | DC), computed by sim/budget.py for the 10 m\nbench link with 2 dBi whips (the DSA then at 5.25 dB, holding the demodulator at -20 dBm); the same numbers as\ndocs/images/block_*.svg." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.3200 45.7200 0) (size 107.9500 7.6200)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d018c236-2c6c-573e-15df-40645929ef7b"))
	(text_box "IP MON: the I window's +\ncomparator through 453\nohm, /10 into 50 ohm (0\n/ 0.33 V): for the\nscope, beside its line\nto the FPGA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 204.4700 90.1700 0) (size 24.1300 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7d7891d5-9dac-5ca3-a0a2-d8db8e4dc197"))
	(text_box "IN MON: the I window's -\ncomparator through 453\nohm, /10 into 50 ohm (0\n/ 0.33 V): for the\nscope, beside its line\nto the FPGA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 204.4700 135.8900 0) (size 24.1300 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "61438928-7911-e80f-9963-84a81f6a67a8"))
	(text_box "QP MON: the Q window's +\ncomparator through 453\nohm, /10 into 50 ohm (0\n/ 0.33 V): for the\nscope, beside its line\nto the FPGA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 204.4700 181.6100 0) (size 25.4000 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8f3dfb9d-4563-52c6-fe32-ca937e30808a"))
	(text_box "QN MON: the Q window's -\ncomparator through 453\nohm, /10 into 50 ohm (0\n/ 0.33 V): for the\nscope, beside its line\nto the FPGA." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 204.4700 227.3300 0) (size 25.4000 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8f227dc1-c1e0-99b7-96d0-c4376cc3de01"))
	(text_box "I_P / I_N, the FAST arm: gain 4, 100 MHz\n(3.5 ns rise) | +-249 mV peak at the\nregulated level | centred 1.65 V | reads\ndown to -81 dBm at the antenna (the\ncomparator floor; noise-quiet would be\n-84) | the data: sign(I)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 41.9100 62.2300 0) (size 38.1000 12.7000)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ac98fd80-3fc5-8da0-e20a-97b117a8a379"))
	(text_box "Q_P / Q_N, the FAST arm: the phase\nerror, 0 at lock, +-249 mV peak off lock\n| DC-100 MHz | centred 1.65 V | a QPSK\nsymbol puts +-176 mV on it" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 41.9100 156.2100 0) (size 39.3700 10.1600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 214 236 255 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ba2e7a06-7350-340e-a23e-09e0051ad0ce"))
	(text_box "LE/HYS (each comparator): both DNP = 3 mV of hysteresis (the\nTLV3601's); fit the 0 ohm = 0 mV, the sharpest edge; fit the\n150 k = 30 mV (56 k = 60 mV), for slow or noisy edges.\nDriving the pin low latches the output." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 129.5400 247.6500 0) (size 55.8800 10.1600)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2ec45c5f-6de3-d135-f5af-2246e2f65675"))
	(text_box "AD5696R (I2C 0x0C): A = V_TQP, B = V_TQN, C\n= V_TIP, D = V_TIN.  16 bits on its own 2.5\nV reference (0.038 mV a step); GAIN low:\n0-2.5 V, round the arms' 1.65 V centre.  It\npowers up at midscale (1.25 V), where all\nfour comparators read high until the FPGA\nwrites them.  VREF is the internal\nreference's output, unused.  The A grade:\nthe threshold servo absorbs its INL and its\nreference's drift." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 307.3400 152.4000 0) (size 43.1800 20.3200)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525) (stroke (width 0) (type default))
		(fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1)) (effects (font (size 1.00 1.00)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7e5b450e-c331-033b-d739-b4cb82ef173d"))
